import{_ as a,o as t,c as s,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.DncwoWA8.js";const i="/projects/ai-skills/diagrams/debug-a-problem.svg",g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Debug an application problem","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Debug an application problem"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"workflows/debug-a-problem.md","filePath":"workflows/debug-a-problem.md"}'),o={name:"workflows/debug-a-problem.md"};function r(p,e,c,l,d,h){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="debug-an-application-problem" tabindex="-1">Debug an application problem <a class="header-anchor" href="#debug-an-application-problem" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Debug an application problem&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Find why an application fails before choosing a correction.</p><p>Start with unexpected behavior, a regression, or a failing test, build, or integration. Finish with an evidence-backed cause and verified fix, or a precise blocker and the next useful observation.</p><h2 id="workflow" tabindex="-1">Workflow <a class="header-anchor" href="#workflow" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Workflow&quot;">​</a></h2><p><img src="'+i+`" alt="Evidence-first diagnosis, regression checks, an authorized correction, and reassessment loops."></p><p><a href="/projects/ai-skills/diagrams/debug-a-problem.html" class="vp-raw">Open interactive diagram</a> · <a href="/projects/ai-skills/diagrams/debug-a-problem.svg">Download SVG</a> · <a href="/projects/ai-skills/diagram-sources/debug-a-problem.json">Editable source</a></p><p>The diagram shows suggested handoffs, not automatic execution or new instruction dependencies. Select a node in the interactive diagram for its source references.</p><details><summary>Read the flow as text</summary><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes catppuccin-latte catppuccin-mocha vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>/systematic-debugging</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Investigate → compare</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Test one hypothesis</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    ├─ unsupported → investigate</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    └─ supported cause</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>           ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Observe a regression failure</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>/coding-with-rules: smallest fix</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    ↓</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Verify → review if selected</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    └─ still failing → investigate</span></span></code></pre></div></details><p>Debugging joins the <a href="/projects/ai-skills/workflows/implement-a-task.html">implementation workflow</a> only after the cause and correction scope are understood. It does not need feature scaffolding by default.</p><h2 id="before-you-start" tabindex="-1">Before you start <a class="header-anchor" href="#before-you-start" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Before you start&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Record expected and observed behavior, the failing action, and the relevant revision and environment. Use sanitized inputs and keep secrets out of diagnostic output.</p><p>Load <a href="/projects/ai-skills/skills/systematic-debugging.html"><code>systematic-debugging</code></a>. Read the target project&#39;s instructions and <a href="/projects/ai-skills/workflows/supporting-tools.html#before-you-start">execution safeguards</a>. Diagnostic edits and state-writing tests need the same authority and workspace protection as other mutations.</p><p>A diagnosis-only request stops at findings. It does not authorize a fix or infrastructure changes.</p><h2 id="steps" tabindex="-1">Steps <a class="header-anchor" href="#steps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Steps&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-bound-the-failure" tabindex="-1">1. Bound the failure <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-bound-the-failure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Bound the failure&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Read the complete relevant error or stack trace. Reproduce the problem with the smallest safe case and record its inputs, preconditions, and frequency.</p><p>Inspect recent changes, but treat timing as a lead rather than proof. Trace the invalid value or state back to its origin. At component boundaries, compare what entered, what left, and the configuration each component used.</p><p>If you cannot reproduce the failure, identify the missing observation. Do not substitute a plausible explanation for evidence.</p><h3 id="_2-compare-and-test-one-explanation" tabindex="-1">2. Compare and test one explanation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-compare-and-test-one-explanation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Compare and test one explanation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Find a working case or a last-known-working revision. Compare inputs, lifecycle, dependencies, ownership, and configuration. If no working comparison exists, use the documented contract and disclose that limit.</p><p>State one falsifiable hypothesis, its prediction, the smallest safe experiment, the observed result, and the next action. Change one relevant variable at a time.</p><p>A rejected hypothesis returns to investigation. An inconclusive result needs better evidence, not a speculative production patch.</p><h3 id="_3-establish-regression-evidence" tabindex="-1">3. Establish regression evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-establish-regression-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. Establish regression evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Before applying the correction, observe a regression test or executable reproduction failing for the intended reason. An existing failing test can already supply this evidence.</p><p>Full <a href="/projects/ai-skills/skills/tdd.html"><code>tdd</code></a> is optional. Regression evidence before the fix is already part of <code>systematic-debugging</code>. If automated coverage is infeasible, explain why and use the strongest safe reproduction available. Do not call manual observation automated coverage.</p><h3 id="_4-correct-the-cause-and-verify" tabindex="-1">4. Correct the cause and verify <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-correct-the-cause-and-verify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4. Correct the cause and verify&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Use <a href="/projects/ai-skills/skills/coding-with-rules.html"><code>coding-with-rules</code></a> for the corrective code or toolchain change. Keep the correction small and exclude unrelated refactoring.</p><p>Rerun the regression case and broader relevant checks. Remove temporary diagnostics you introduced unless they belong in the final fix, then rerun affected checks.</p><p>For intermittent problems, report trial counts and conditions. One passing run is not proof that flakiness is gone. Use <a href="/projects/ai-skills/workflows/supporting-tools.html#review-an-existing-change">independent code review</a> when requested and supported.</p><h3 id="_5-reassess-when-the-evidence-changes" tabindex="-1">5. Reassess when the evidence changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-reassess-when-the-evidence-changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5. Reassess when the evidence changes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>If the fix fails, return to investigation. After three failed corrective attempts at the same unresolved failure, stop patching and reassess the reproduction, assumptions, environment, coupling, and architecture.</p><p>This count concerns corrective attempts, not ordinary diagnostic observations. Architectural changes still require owner agreement. Return to <a href="/projects/ai-skills/workflows/plan-a-project.html">planning</a> if the demonstrated cause requires broader scope or changed behavior.</p><h2 id="example-an-exported-name-creates-an-extra-column" tabindex="-1">Example: an exported name creates an extra column <a class="header-anchor" href="#example-an-exported-name-creates-an-extra-column" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Example: an exported name creates an extra column&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is an illustrative failure in the reporting project, not an observed defect in this collection.</p><p>A name containing a comma, such as <code>North, West</code>, appears as two CSV columns. A useful initial request is:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes catppuccin-latte catppuccin-mocha vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>Diagnose why exporting the name &quot;North, West&quot; produces an extra column.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Use /systematic-debugging. Compare it with a name without a comma and trace</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>the serialized field through the existing export path. Report the supported</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>cause and a bounded correction proposal before editing.</span></span></code></pre></div><p>If inspection supports incorrect field escaping as the cause, the next authorized phase should establish a failing export test before changing the serializer. The expected result is one preserved name field and unchanged unrelated export behavior.</p><p>If the serializer is correct but the consuming application misreads the file, investigate that boundary instead. Do not change quoting merely because it was the first hypothesis.</p><h2 id="report-the-result" tabindex="-1">Report the result <a class="header-anchor" href="#report-the-result" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Report the result&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Separate the demonstrated cause, corrective change, verification, and remaining uncertainty. Report any temporary containment separately from the root-cause fix.</p><p>An authorized rollback can contain an incident without proving its cause. Leave the diagnosis open until the evidence supports it.</p><p>For a diagnosis-only procedure, see <a href="/projects/ai-skills/workflows/diagnose-a-failure.html">Find the root cause before proposing a fix</a>.</p>`,42)])])}const f=a(o,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,f as default};
